I suppose what you get from the mixture is pretty much the same effect
as if you were to drink all those potions individually (which you can do)
Invisible for a long time, blind for quite a while, and if the hallucination
somehow manages to last longer than the blindness, loads of fun.

One possible use of mixtures, however, might be to add blessed and cursed
potions to get uncursed results.  After all, what good is a blessed potion
of confusion if you can't uncurse your potion of gain ability?  Just be
careful that you add the blessed to the curse (avoid the acid to water
explosion.)

Now, if we really wanted to cause problems for the game designers:
if enchantments can have any range of + or -, how about a PH level for
bless/cursedness?  It wouldn't have to have any effects on the item
itself (blessed by 8 = blessed by 1), but would determine how
resistant something is to being blessed or cursed.  It would take
five remove curse scrolls to get rid of those cursed (-5) gloves of
fumbling.

Not to mention the wonderful explosion you get from mixing a
+6 potion with a -6 potion.   Side effect of earthquake+tower of flame?


